<!--
    A folded switch is never printed where a condition belongs.  P8
    "region structurer" (switch-case schema, `try_switch_cases`); a strict
    correctness fix with no option.

    `scan` loops over a string with a jump-table switch.  Every case but
    `'w'..'z'` advances and continues the loop; `'w'..'z'` runs an inner loop
    over the run of such characters before it continues.  The region
    structurer folded the switch while that inner loop was still unfolded,
    taking the inner loop's head as the switch's exit and keeping the other
    cases' backedges as a second successor of the folded switch.  The `if`
    schema then took the folded switch for a condition: kuna printed the
    switch, then `if` on a line of its own, then the whole switch again as the
    condition, then the inner loop as the `if` body.  The structurer now waits
    for the inner loop to fold into its case, and the function prints as the
    source wrote it.

    #1 no `if` or `while` without its condition; #2 one switch; #3 the inner
    loop inside its case; #4 the outer loop around the switch.

    gcc 11.4 -O0 -fno-pie -no-pie -fcf-protection=none
    -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -nostdlib -static -Wl,-Ttext=0x401000
    (x86-64) of

        __attribute__((noinline)) void sink(int v) { __asm__ volatile("" :: "r"(v)); }

        int scan(const char *s, int *out)
        {
            int n = 0;
            while (*s && *s != '.') {
                switch (*s) {
                case 'a': sink(1); s++; break;
                case 'b': sink(2); s++; break;
                case 'c': sink(3); s += 2; break;
                case 'd': n++; s++; break;
                case 'e': n += 2; s++; break;
                case 'w': case 'x': case 'y': case 'z': {
                    int i = 0;
                    while (*s >= 'w' && *s <= 'z') { i = i * 4 + *s - 'w'; s++; }
                    out[n & 7] = i;
                    break;
                }
                default: s++; break;
                }
            }
            return n;
        }
        void _start(void) {}

    The jump table is the .rodata chunk at 0x402000.
-->
